    {
      "id": "p0112-b010",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Laughter doesn't always translate perfectly between languages, so localizers sometimes need to adjust the way characters laugh to sound more natural in the target language. As an example, Sans' standard \"heheh\" laugh in the English script was tweaked on a per-scene basis to match the different moods Toby had intended:",
        "raw": "Laughter doesn't always translate perfectly between languages, so localizers\nsometimes need to adjust the way characters laugh to sound more natural in the\ntarget language. As an example, Sans' standard \"heheh\" laugh in the English script\nwas tweaked on a per-scene basis to match the different moods Toby had intended:",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29665973,
          0.46532857,
          0.90678875,
          0.53231429
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.29221524,
          0.46461429,
          0.90882751,
          0.53338571
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          18,
          19,
          20,
          21
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "笑声并不总能在语言之间直接照搬，所以本地化人员有时需要调整角色的笑法，让它在目标语言中更自然。例如，英语剧本中 Sans 惯常的“heheh”，就按场景逐一调整，以贴合 Toby 想要的不同气氛：",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
